### 1. Layout

Read: `coding-playbook/client/components.md` — sections "Page Layout Pattern" and "Styling Rules", `coding-playbook/client/seo.md` — section "1. Skip-to-Main Link (WCAG 2.4.1 Bypass Blocks)"

Traces to: brief #1; learn desired 1 (site top bar and footer, docs prose styles, no sidebar, a single reading-width column); undesired 1; brief open question 5 (resolved: the docs body width is reused). Every value is one the docs layout already uses (`src/app/docs/layout.tsx`: `paddingTop: 40`, `paddingBottom: 80`, inner `maxWidth: 1000`, `px-[20px] md:px-[64px]`), so the section introduces no new spacing.

- [x] Create `layout.tsx` (server component): `<a href="#main" className="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>`, `<TopBar sticky />` (no `active`: /learn is not a nav destination), `<main id="main" className="flex justify-center" style={{ paddingTop: 40, paddingBottom: 80 }}>` holding `<div className="w-full px-[20px] md:px-[64px]" style={{ maxWidth: 1000 }}>{children}</div>`, then `<Footer />`. JSDoc: why this is not the docs layout (no sidebar; docsRegistry renders only package markdown) nor the /brain layout (brain palette and footer).
